{"ts": "2026-11-07T10:48:42.940239Z", "run_id": "r-20261107T1029Z-c307", "unit": "openspec:add-taint-runtime", "seq": 8, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-001", "id": "Q-001", "status": "answered", "reason": "Verified in the repository: analyze.ts line 396 writes edge.ref as refToString(ref) (bare text); the frozen analyze.test.ts line 230 asserts invoiceId.ref equals \"inputs.invoice_id\", so the stored form cannot be wrapped; refs.ts scanTemplate pushes a text segment when no \"${{\" is found and otherwise trims the content and calls parseRef, so the wrapped form yields parseRef(edge.ref). The test at runtime-references.test.ts:299 therefore cannot pass as written, and the suggested one-line change is the minimal fix that keeps the spec's wording (scanTemplate on edge.ref) and touches no production code. Task 1.2 is the red/green task that owns this test file, not a fix task, so accepting the suggestion to unfreeze it is appropriate.", "called": true, "tasks": ["1.2"], "target": null, "kind": "technical", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 0.92288025, "decision": "accept", "answer_sha256": "c579db4f9f1da56e82c62a4701881e48bf8153b926558ec160890d1bd7d53266", "checked": [{"ref": "src/authoring/taint/runtime-references.test.ts:299", "quote": "const seg = scanTemplate(edge.ref).find((candidate) => candidate.type === \"ref\");", "claim": "The test passes the bare edge ref text to scanTemplate, which yields no ref segment."}, {"ref": "src/authoring/taint/analyze.ts:396", "quote": "ref: ref !== undefined ? refToString(ref) : occurrence.raw,", "claim": "analyzeTaint stores edge.ref as the unwrapped refToString text."}, {"ref": "src/authoring/taint/analyze.test.ts:230", "quote": "assert.equal(invoiceId.ref, \"inputs.invoice_id\");", "claim": "The frozen test pins edge.ref to the unwrapped form, so the implementation cannot wrap it."}, {"ref": "src/authoring/format/refs.ts:93", "quote": "const open = text.indexOf(\"${{\", i);", "claim": "scanTemplate only recognises references opened by ${{ and treats other text as a text segment."}, {"ref": "src/authoring/format/refs.ts:105", "quote": "const content = text.slice(open + 3, close).trim();", "claim": "Wrapping the edge text in ${{ }} makes scanTemplate trim it and hand exactly edge.ref to parseRef."}, {"ref": "spec:specs/taint/spec.md#scenario-analyzetaint-and-the-shared-rules-agree-on-rf-1", "quote": "`referenceTaint(ref, taintOf)` for every edge (`ref` from `scanTemplate` on `edge.ref`)", "claim": "The scenario means the parsed Ref of the edge text, which the wrapped scanTemplate call produces."}, {"ref": "openspec/changes/add-taint-runtime/tasks.md:4", "quote": "Write `src/authoring/taint/runtime-references.test.ts` first", "claim": "Task 1.2 owns this test file, so the change is to the task's own red test rather than another unit's frozen file."}]}
